Check that a read-only access to a remote table from a statement that writes
locally (i.e. UPDATE local ... WHERE x > (SELECT max(x) FROM remdb.t)) does not
create a remote transaction (remtran), and that a remote transaction is still
created for, and joined after, an actual write to the remote db.

The base configuration disables push, so remote writes use remtran; the
fdbpush variant enables push writes, and no remtran is expected at all.
